of the above could be the graph of $y = x(x + 1)(x - 1)$?" :question/worked-solution "Based on the factored equation, we can make the following conclusions about the graph:\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the roots $x=0,\\pm 1$ is $1,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at these points. Moreover, because $x=0,\\pm 1$ are simple roots, the graph must *not* be tangent to the $x$-axis at these points.\n\nOnly the graphs $\\text{II}$ and $\\text{IV}$ satisfy these conditions.\n\nTo choose between these two graphs, we need to consider the end behavior. Since the leading coefficient is positive, as $x$ approaches $\\infty ,$ $y$ approaches $\\infty .$ Since only graph $\\text{IV}$ displays this end behavior, the correct answer is $\\text{IV}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129621 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d03ac24f-82a6-5af8-b1b8-9021e521d47a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Graph of a Factored Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8255180d-a404-5bc2-b945-0ee2962afe4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "IV" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127521} {:answer/id #uuid "b3023afd-f7df-5f0a-86ee-20df7d9fdffd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127522} {:answer/id #uuid "ece6368a-6af3-5227-957f-f83b33abf1cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "II" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127523} {:answer/id #uuid "fbddabbe-8d21-5026-a9ff-5a93ddc1197a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the given graphs are correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127524} {:answer/id #uuid "4f2f774d-86d1-5ed4-8f83-a01b65e68875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8255180d-a404-5bc2-b945-0ee2962afe4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "IV" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127521} :answer-field/id #uuid "329e2aaa-1039-5321-a9e5-307597a48dea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127520}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a258d53-768b-53db-ad8c-9114ea48f386" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-38632" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2049/Source/Images/q-38632.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y =-5x^{2}(x - 1)^{2}(x - 2)$?" :question/worked-solution "Based on the factored equation, we can make the following conclusions about the graph:\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=2$ is $1,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at this point. Moreover, because $x=2$ is a simple root, the graph must *not* be tangent to the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the roots $x=0,1$ is $2,$ which is even, the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at these points.\n\nOnly the graphs $\\text{I}$ and $\\text{IV}$ satisfy these conditions.\n\nTo choose between these two graphs, we need to consider the end behavior. Since the leading coefficient is negative, as $x$ approaches $\\infty ,$ $y$ approaches $-\\infty .$\n\nOnly graph $\\text{IV}$ displays this end behavior. Therefore, the correct answer is $\\text{IV}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129630 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fc09a0f-34d3-5ca9-9964-6cb00498bfa7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Factored Polynomial Shown in a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cd02eed-7414-5093-8143-80d7d06bced0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 3(x + 3)(x + 1)(x - 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127575} {:answer/id #uuid "8ddc70c0-43b1-5990-9b32-9f0281610ac6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = (x + 3)(x + 1)^{2}(x - 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127576} {:answer/id #uuid "ab334cff-f365-5cc1-afc0-8f879d26b79b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 3(x + 2)(x + 1)(x - 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127577} {:answer/id #uuid "0f098122-7849-5b1f-97da-66b7acd058bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 2(x + 3)(x + 1)(x - 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127578} {:answer/id #uuid "69627e2a-df43-5213-a339-4fd55ef796cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 5x^{2}(x + 1)(x - 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ddc70c0-43b1-5990-9b32-9f0281610ac6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = (x + 3)(x + 1)^{2}(x - 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127576} :answer-field/id #uuid "697da19f-d951-5e95-a8d4-f0464cd071d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127574}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50ca6d21-0417-5001-b5a6-6f3285a4ca2f" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-38671" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2049/Source/Images/q-38671.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the equation of the polynomial curve shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice that the function has precisely three distinct roots, $x=-3,$ $x=-1,$ and $x=2.$\n\nBased on the graph, we can make the following conclusions about the multiplicities of the roots:\n\n- Since the graph is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=-3,$ this root is a simple root (the multiplicity equals $1$).\n\n- Since the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=-1,$ this root has even multiplicity.\n\n- Since the graph is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=2,$ this root is a simple root (the multiplicity equals $1$).\n\nFrom the given options, the only possible equation is $y=(x+3)(x+1{)}^{2}(x-2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20d36a72-f50d-5f0c-b0fe-8dfca7aa7246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244360} {:answer/id #uuid "c421830f-d672-591f-936f-7841571e829e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244361} {:answer/id #uuid "4b1ff5c9-ae03-5578-886d-cf9c77888723" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244362} {:answer/id #uuid "a84e8d3d-325f-55fb-be6f-c332072f47ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244363} {:answer/id #uuid "760d168b-bd98-548a-9e1a-836ac1db5d5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c421830f-d672-591f-936f-7841571e829e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244361} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ac26998-6f00-53e0-a2de-939d74eed232" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244359}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dabea786-8408-5b31-8a47-8665b8cf6666" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-38680" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/682105815047990048e100ea59c2652e48c0deea8c8caa422bfe3efca7d11c65.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are correct?\n\n- $p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n- $x=-1$ is a simple root.\n- $x=2$ is a root of even multiplicity." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. As $x$ moves right in the positive direction towards $+\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves down in the negative direction towards $-\\infty .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The root $x=-1$ is not a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at the point, and the curve is tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement III is false. The root $x=2$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244365 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91c7665b-dc1f-5993-bdb5-ada5a628c6ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244367} {:answer/id #uuid "634fa41b-ef7b-5cdf-beac-c1b09c11be81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244368} {:answer/id #uuid "a8dbeb37-33df-5d3b-80c0-216f5fcb7163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244369} {:answer/id #uuid "e929f0c8-5c8b-5193-a302-1e196359bac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244370} {:answer/id #uuid "ceba779f-eaca-5bbc-909c-2c40614b9849" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8dbeb37-33df-5d3b-80c0-216f5fcb7163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244369} :answer-field/id #uuid "c64e3073-6eed-5ac0-91b7-b58edfded72c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244366}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5524fa1-4ea1-5462-b6a2-7b0a96647502" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-38770" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/cd19717bd41b787346a96394ce3bc4e38fe690340bb73bd3d11139d41ff977e2.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=2$ is a simple root.\n- $x=-1$ is a root of even multiplicity.\n- $p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The root $x=2$ is a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at the point and the curve is not tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The root $x=-1$  has an even multiplicity because at $x=-1$ the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction.\n\n- Statement III is false. As $x$ moves right in the positive direction towards $+\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves up in the positive direction towards $+\\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244372 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fc09a0f-34d3-5ca9-9964-6cb00498bfa7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Factored Polynomial Shown in a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0ed54ff-3a8e-59bb-ab41-aeb5cc3d5de6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}(x+4{)}^{5}(x+2{)}^{2}(x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244374} {:answer/id #uuid "85eb56d5-df90-5cf3-a9ed-96fc0feb1dc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{5}(x+2{)}^{2}(x+1{)}^{2}(x-2{)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244375} {:answer/id #uuid "a8baf4e4-3433-50a3-b44d-fc597f9cd95c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=10(x+2{)}^{6}(x+1{)}^{4}(x-2{)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244376} {:answer/id #uuid "89fb66b6-d949-5222-ab21-ddf485ed1397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{10}(x+2{)}^{2}(x+1)(x-2{)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244377} {:answer/id #uuid "531c80de-4840-5592-8ac2-4a4901d27558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{3}(x+2{)}^{4}(x+1)(x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89fb66b6-d949-5222-ab21-ddf485ed1397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{10}(x+2{)}^{2}(x+1)(x-2{)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244377} :answer-field/id #uuid "515505f6-ff6b-5116-bb3f-70c129ca3056" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244373}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f246307-d10c-5546-bdff-74bd4d87017a" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-38774" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/eb53a2c5235dacb8a88c4a686cb24e51320d5370fc3d7cd5265f888c4d54802c.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the equation of the polynomial curve shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice that the function has precisely three distinct roots, $x=-2,$ $x=-1,$ and $x=2.$\n\nBased on the graph, we can make the following conclusions about the multiplicities of the roots:\n\n- Since the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=-2,$ this root has even multiplicity.\n\n- Since the graph is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=-1,$ this root is a simple root (the multiplicity equals $1$).\n\n- Since the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=2,$ this root has even multiplicity.\n\nFrom the given options, the only possible equation is $y=\\frac{1}{10}(x+2{)}^{2}(x+1)(x-2{)}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244379 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7aff6877-a713-57b2-a91b-7b11fc476f70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244381} {:answer/id #uuid "0856df4b-1279-5389-a45a-964387b4130d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244382} {:answer/id #uuid "06571f84-b72a-5276-a527-af8995363009" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I,II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244383} {:answer/id #uuid "032b7a19-96dc-5ccb-8ae9-732b0221dd45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244384} {:answer/id #uuid "f3f31ce2-8a9e-52ee-8856-f5501b29378e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "032b7a19-96dc-5ccb-8ae9-732b0221dd45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244384} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca0fb778-45cf-5964-8596-9c7f582f3631" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244380}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09779689-0cd4-5943-b116-c07ec9ff5f57" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-80302" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/1f49d3448340c612269cdeea20680d717c736cb9a19fcf83dac86da1e4a6127f.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=-1$ is a simple root.\n- $x=2$ is a root of odd multiplicity.\n- $x=2$ is a simple root." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The root $x=-1$ is a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at the point and the curve is not tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The root $x=2$ has an odd multiplicity because at $x=2$ the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Statement III is false. The root $x=2$ is not a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at that point, and the curve is tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244386 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad4d25ba-c0bc-513e-bfb6-861b79a5f728" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244388} {:answer/id #uuid "13aba830-b445-5607-bfb3-d276b38f0ff0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244389} {:answer/id #uuid "b5ef9e97-aa7f-5815-b914-486e751f3282" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244390} {:answer/id #uuid "f7c69bde-0ca6-54c8-8c29-ec7723099a86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244391} {:answer/id #uuid "d35f02c4-7983-53d4-9166-a7b112563ba8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d35f02c4-7983-53d4-9166-a7b112563ba8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244392} :answer-field/id #uuid "50c528ef-945c-5b58-bf6a-8a7b821c6038" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244387}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "91d3ac9b-2d2d-5160-bd5c-1e34a396139a" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-80303" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/0a7b19b50822235a2dcbfcdf74984735a1e26b2b775180b24bdc2bcbf24c588b.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=-2$ is a root of even multiplicity.\n- $x=1$ is **not** a simple root.\n- $x=1$ is a root of even multiplicity." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The root $x=-2$ has an odd multiplicity because at $x=-2$ the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The root $x=1$ is not a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at that point, and the curve is tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement III is false. The root $x=1$ has an odd multiplicity because at $x=1$ the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244393 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fc09a0f-34d3-5ca9-9964-6cb00498bfa7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Factored Polynomial Shown in a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f56b4e8-db5b-53e8-9898-e19530aa1b66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x{(x+1)}^{2}(x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244395} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6c9ec4-27ce-52ec-acf3-2c32134df0ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}(x+1)(x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244396} {:answer/id #uuid "233364d7-d8d9-5fdc-a443-5e488babb343" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}(x+1){(x-2)}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244397} {:answer/id #uuid "85958731-a749-5094-a6e4-8cdba99c4591" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{5}{(x+1)}^{2}(x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244398} {:answer/id #uuid "be7807ef-5f84-5642-a875-1ff93830